; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Truchet Tiles
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     tiles, ARC, random, grid, patterns
; SUMMARY:  Covers the screen with randomly turned tiles of quarter circles that join into winding paths.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Every square tile has two quarter circles on it, in opposite
;   corners. A tile can sit one of two ways. Choosing at random for
;   each tile still gives smooth paths, because every quarter circle
;   meets its neighbor in the middle of an edge. The pen color shifts
;   across the screen so the paths glow from teal to pink.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run for a new maze of curves. Change :tile for bigger or
;   smaller tiles.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * ARC: a curve drawn around the turtle without moving it
;   * nested FOR loops for a grid
;   * a coin toss with RANDOM 2
;   * why local rules can make a pattern that looks planned
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make every tile the same way round. What do you get?
;   * Use (random 4) and four kinds of tiles, some with straight lines.
;   * Make the pen as wide as half a tile.
; ============================================================

; QUARTER draws a quarter circle centered on the corner (x, y),
; sweeping clockwise from :heading. Its radius is half a tile, so it
; touches the middles of the two edges that meet at that corner.
to quarter :x :y :heading
  penup setxy :x :y setheading :heading pendown
  arc 90 :tile / 2
end

; TILE draws the two quarter circles of the tile whose bottom left
; corner is (x, y), one way round or the other.
to tile :x :y
  localmake "t :tile
  ; Color from teal on the left to pink on the right.
  localmake "mix (:x + 400) / 800
  setpencolor (list 40 + 210 * :mix 200 - 90 * :mix 190)
  ifelse 0 = random 2 [
    ; bottom left and top right corners
    quarter :x :y 0
    quarter :x + :t :y + :t 180
  ] [
    ; top left and bottom right corners
    quarter :x :y + :t 90
    quarter :x + :t :y 270
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [20 20 35]
make "tile 40
setpensize 6
for [y -300 260 :tile] [
  for [x -400 360 :tile] [tile :x :y]
]
